msgid "``V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_DECODER_SLICE_INTERFACE (boolean)``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/ext-ctrls-codec.rst:712
msgid ""
"If enabled the decoder expects to receive a single slice per buffer, "
"otherwise the decoder expects a single frame in per buffer. Applicable to "
"the decoder, all codecs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/ext-ctrls-codec.rst:716
msgid "``V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_DEC_DISPLAY_DELAY_ENABLE (boolean)``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/ext-ctrls-codec.rst:717
msgid ""
"If the display delay is enabled then the decoder is forced to return a "
"CAPTURE buffer (decoded frame) after processing a certain number of OUTPUT "
"buffers. The delay can be set through "
"``V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_DEC_DISPLAY_DELAY``. This feature can be used for "
"example for generating thumbnails of videos. Applicable to the decoder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/ext-ctrls-codec.rst:724
msgid "``V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_DEC_DISPLAY_DELAY (integer)``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/ext-ctrls-codec.rst:725
msgid ""
"Display delay value for decoder. The decoder is forced to return a decoded "
"frame after the set 'display delay' number of frames. If this number is low "
"it may result in frames returned out of display order, in addition the "
"hardware may still be using the returned buffer as a reference picture for "
"subsequent frames."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/ext-ctrls-codec.rst:731
msgid "``V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_AU_DELIMITER (boolean)``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/ext-ctrls-codec.rst:732
msgid ""
"If enabled then, AUD (Access Unit Delimiter) NALUs will be generated. That "
"could be useful to find the start of a frame without having to fully parse "
"each NALU. Applicable to the H264 and HEVC encoders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/ext-ctrls-codec.rst:736
msgid "``V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_H264_VUI_SAR_ENABLE (boolean)``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/ext-ctrls-codec.rst:737
msgid ""
"Enable writing sample aspect ratio in the Video Usability Information. "
"Applicable to the H264 encoder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/ext-ctrls-codec.rst:740
msgid "``V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_BACKGROUND_DETECTION (boolean)``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/ext-ctrls-codec.rst:741
msgid ""
"If enabled, the encoder detect a background region in frame and use low bits "
"or skip mode to encode the background region. If a lot of scenes are "
"stationary or background, It may help to reduce the video bitrate. "
"Applicable to the encoder."
msgstr ""

